# Code for "which k benchmarks to run on a new model"

Everything here is CPU-only Python. The downloaded leaderboard files are not shipped and must be re-downloaded from the pinned sources below; what is shipped
is derived: `results/data_out/*.npz` (dense score matrices, 0.6 MB in total), the tidy `results/*.csv` and the per-run pickles `results/raw/` (20 MB, Git LFS).
Paths below are relative to the delivery root `$R`. The figures and tables are drawn from `results/*.csv` by the scripts delivered with them (`figures/src`, `tables/`). The repository carries no author or
institution identifiers.

## Environment
Python 3.11.2, numpy 2.4.6, scipy 1.17.1, pandas 3.0.6, scikit-learn 1.9.1, pyarrow 26.0.0 (pinned in `code/requirements.txt`; `pip install -r code/requirements.txt`).
Nothing needs a GPU. Single-thread BLAS is used inside jobs (`OMP_NUM_THREADS=1`).

