Main runs used `n_draws=200` random draws, `n_part=5` target partitions per fold, 10 outer folds (grouped by family; random and time-forward as variants).
Seeds: 11000 (mteb_eng), 12000 (mteb_multi), 13000 (helm_mmlu) plus fold and draw indices; the bootstrap uses seed 0. Each main run takes 5-20 CPU minutes
(the `seconds` field of every pickle records it); the history sweeps take roughly an hour per dataset on one core.

## What the code computes (the short version)

* `bmk/fa.py`: factor analysis by EM (noise floor 0.05; rank by inner 5-fold held-out likelihood, one-SE rule), masked-EM variant for missing cells.
* `bmk/select_predict.py`: selectors (random, greedy A, greedy D, max-variance, one-factor, pivoted QR, leverage, k-medoids, test-leaking oracle) and predictors
  (column mean, one-factor, ridge, kNN, Ledoit-Wolf conditioning, factor model, fold-in Soft-Impute).
* `bmk/protocol.py`: the leakage-free protocol. Everything fitted (standardisation, transform, factor model, selector, predictor tuning) uses training rows only;
  held-out models never influence it. Errors are always on the original standardised scale after back-transform.
* `aggregate.py`: closure curves, k* with family-bootstrap intervals, the H2 gap with a family-clustered bootstrap (B=2000; for the organisation-grouped split the clusters are organisations), H1 outcome table, extras.
* `code/DEVIATIONS.md` lists every departure from the Brief; the paper must state them.

